  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aircraft Manufacturing (NAICS 336411) had $36B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The market recorded 4,600 awards with an average award size of $7.8M. Obligations are down 41.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer with $35.4B in obligations, leaving only modest participation from other agencies such as the Department of Homeland Security with $137M and the Department of Commerce with $108M. Lockheed Martin Corporation and The Boeing Company lead vendors in this space, with $9.3B and multiple Boeing entries totaling several large awards including $5.9B, $3.6B, $2.4B, $1.6B, and $1.5B. Sikorsky Aircraft Corporation and Bell Textron Inc follow with $2.5B and $1.8B respectively. FY2026 to date obligations of $36B compare with prior full fiscal years of $61.2B in FY25 and $44.2B in FY24, after earlier totals of $60.1B in FY23, $37.2B in FY22, and $40.7B in FY21. These figures reflect fiscal year to date totals and partial current-year reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
